<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhoja II of Kolhapur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1175–1212</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhoja II was the last major king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silahara-dynasty">Shilahara dynasty</a> of Kolhapur in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. As the power of the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> and Kalachuris collapsed in the late twelfth century, he ruled independently and took imperial titles. Around 1212 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yadava">Yadava</a> king Singhana conquered Kolhapur, ending the dynasty.</p></div>
